.TH "HTMLTABLEELEMENT.DELETECAPTION" "3JS" "August 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLTableElement.deleteCaption \- HTMLTableElement: deleteCaption()
method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]deleteCaption()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]HTMLTableElement\f[R] interface removes the first
\f[CR]<caption>\f[R] element child from a given \f[CR]<table>\f[R], if
any.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
deleteCaption()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SH EXAMPLES
This example uses JavaScript to delete a table\(cqs caption.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]table\f[R]>
  <\f[B]caption\f[R]>
    This caption will be deleted!
  </\f[B]caption\f[R]>
  <\f[B]tbody\f[R]>
    <\f[B]tr\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 1.1</\f[B]td\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 1.2</\f[B]td\f[R]>
    </\f[B]tr\f[R]>
    <\f[B]tr\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 2.1</\f[B]td\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 2.2</\f[B]td\f[R]>
    </\f[B]tr\f[R]>
  </\f[B]tbody\f[R]>
</\f[B]table\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] table = document.querySelector(\(dqtable\(dq);
table.deleteCaption();
.EE
.SS Result
